# Bounce on OpenFL with $Time

Same window as `bounce_openfl.wcn`, but the clock lives in the game. Target ticks `Time`; Game moves because `$` notifies. Do not also call `Game::update!` from `%step`.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball $Time
PlayArea = Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
Time = Int/t
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea 800 600]
  [:Ball 200 150 6 5 16]
  [:Time 0]
]
```

## Methods

```
Ball::bounced = { PlayArea/r |
  ndx = if ((x < 0) or (x > r.width)) { -dx  } else { dx }.
  ndy = if ((y < 0) or (y > r.height)) { -dy } else { dy }.
  [:Ball (x+ndx) (y+ndy) ndx ndy rad]
}

Time::update! = { [:Time (t + 1)] }

Game::update! = {
  [:Game playArea ball.bounced(playArea) time]
}

Ball::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  g.beginFill(0xffffff).drawCircle(x, y, rad).endFill()
}

PlayArea::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  g.beginFill(0x003300).drawRect(0, 0, width, height).endFill()
}


Game::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  drawnPA = playArea.draw(g).
  drawnBal = ball.draw(g).
  this
}
```

## Target

```
%openfl

%init
var game:Game;

function init():Void {
    game = GameAssemblage.factory();
}

%step
function step():Void {
    wchntGraphics.clear();
    // this updates the timer. 
    // And because of the dependency relationship between timer and game, 
    // that triggers update!() on game 
    game.time.update_mutates();
    game.draw(wchntGraphics);
}
```
